  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 1028 PM CST Tue Nov 24 2026\n\nLong range forecast models seem keen on keeping an active upper \nlevel pattern for the next couple of weeks. While these systems do \nnot seem favorable for precipitation for the next 7 days, we may be \nsubject to fluctuating temperatures due to the potential for multiple \nfrontal passages through the High Plains.\n\nMost of the extended period should be near or above average both for \nlow and high temperatures. On days where a cold front moves \nthrough, namely this Sunday, expected high temperatures to fall \nbelow normal. Otherwise, a quick recovery to the 60s is forecast \ndue to heights rebuilding over the CWA alongside surface winds \nreturning to southwesterly flow. \n\nRangel",
